# Tests that exercise features beamlet leaves out by design. One module per line, then why.
# Anything not listed here must pass (or is a bug to fix).

# Ports to programs run (with --exec, see <Module>.args); these two differ by design.
echo                          prints a port's number, which BEAM counts apart from pids
test_close_console_driver     opens AtomVM's "console" driver: on a host, a missing program whose error output races the result

# There is no distribution: another node's pids, refs and ports do not decode.
test_ets                      decodes pids and ports of other nodes
test_node                     decodes a pid, a ref and a port of another node; its local checks are erlang/node_local
test_binary_to_term           decodes other nodes' pids, refs and ports, wants BEAM's <0.1.0> alive, opens a port and a socket; the rest is erlang/binary_to_term_local

# Need files AtomVM's build generates (packs, .hrl data, the JIT target macro); to_hrl is a build script.
test_add_avm_pack_binary      AtomVM build output
test_add_avm_pack_file        AtomVM build output
test_close_avm_pack           AtomVM build output
test_code_get_object_code     AtomVM build output
test_code_load_abs            AtomVM build output
test_code_load_binary         AtomVM build output
test_stacktrace               AtomVM build output
to_hrl                        not a test

# zlib's compressed bytes are C zlib's own; miniz_oxide's are valid deflate, but not the same bytes.
test_zlib_compress            compares compressed bytes with C zlib's

# BEAM's per-process heap: beamlet has no per-process heaps (reference-counted terms).
memlimit                      heap sizes
test_gc                       heap sizes
test_min_heap_size            heap sizes
test_refc_binaries            heap sizes
test_throw_call_ext_last      heap sizes

# OTP's code server's internals: beamlet's code server is its own (beamlet_code), with no code_server table.
test_code_server_nifs         calls code_server:is_loaded/1, which reads the code_server ETS table
